    <bpmn:process id="W_W3666" name="W3666. Regulated-Product Identification &amp; BPS Standards Mapping" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Program strategy (W3665); assortment change; new BPS standard
Frequency: Maintained + on change
Volume: DTI-BPS-regulated SKU subset (~10,000–15,000 SKUs across regulated categories)
Owner: Product Compliance Manager / Merchandising
Participants: Product Compliance Manager, Merchandising (links to VS-01), MDM (links to VS-29.1), Quality (links to VS-31), Vendor Mgmt (links to VS-03)
Source: workflow W3666 — Regulated-Product Identification &amp; BPS Standards Mapping</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3666_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3666_Lane1" name="Product Compliance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3666_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3666_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3666_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3666_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3666_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3666_Start3" name="Program strategy (W3665); assortment change; new BPS standard">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3666_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3666_Task4" name="Product Compliance Manager/Merchandising maintain the regulated-product…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Product Compliance Manager/Merchandising maintain the regulated-product register: identify which of the 35,000 active SKUs fall under DTI-BPS mandatory certification (PNS-covered products), map each to its governing Philippine National Standard (PNS) and DAO, the certification type required (PS Mark / ICC / SOC / exempt), and the certificate/sticker obligation; integrate to item master (links to VS-29.1) with a &quot;regulated&quot; flag and cert-required attribute
Responsible (R): Product Compliance Manager / Merchandising / MDM
Accountable (A): Product Compliance Manager
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3666_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3666_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3666_Task5" name="Product Compliance Manager classify each regulated SKU by origin (locally…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Product Compliance Manager classify each regulated SKU by origin (locally manufactured → vendor PS License; imported → ICC per shipment or SOC), certification status, and risk tier (high-risk structural/electrical vs. lower-risk); drive the standards mapping into assortment and sourcing decisions (links to VS-01/VS-03)
Responsible (R): Product Compliance Manager / Merchandising
Accountable (A): Product Compliance Manager
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3666_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3666_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3666_Task6" name="Product Compliance Manager/MDM enforce the regulated flag downstream: gate PO…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Product Compliance Manager/MDM enforce the regulated flag downstream: gate PO creation, goods receipt, and POS saleability on certification status (links to W3669/W3681), and publish the regulated-product register to compliance, merchandising, and audit (links to W3672)
Responsible (R): Product Compliance Manager / MDM
Accountable (A): Product Compliance Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3666_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3666_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3666_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3666_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-580 (ensure controlled execution — PS Mark Licensing, Vendor Certification &amp; Product Standards Governance (PA-117.1).) | - operational: standards mapping and MDM governance; operational: assortment compliance gate (W3669)
Owner: Product Compliance Manager / Merchandising</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3666_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3666_Annotation8" targetRef="W3666_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3666_Flow10" sourceRef="W3666_Start3" targetRef="W3666_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3666_Flow11" sourceRef="W3666_Task4" targetRef="W3666_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3666_Flow12" sourceRef="W3666_Task5" targetRef="W3666_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3666_Flow13" sourceRef="W3666_Task6" targetRef="W3666_End7" />
    </bpmn:process>
