    <bpmn:process id="W_W3669" name="W3669. New-Product Certification &amp; Assortment Compliance Gate" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New-product introduction / assortment onboarding (links to VS-01.1/W705)
Frequency: Per new regulated SKU
Volume: ~5–8% annual SKU growth on regulated categories
Owner: Product Compliance Manager / Merchandising
Participants: Product Compliance Manager, Merchandising (links to VS-01), Vendor Mgmt (links to VS-03), Quality (links to VS-31), Import (links to VS-02.2/VS-87), MDM (links to VS-29.1)
Source: workflow W3669 — New-Product Certification &amp; Assortment Compliance Gate</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3669_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3669_Lane1" name="Product Compliance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3669_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3669_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3669_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3669_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3669_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3669_Start3" name="New-product introduction / assortment onboarding (links to VS-01.1/W705)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3669_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3669_Task4" name="Product Compliance Manager/Merchandising assess every new product at assortment…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Product Compliance Manager/Merchandising assess every new product at assortment stage (links to VS-01.1 sample evaluation) for DTI-BPS regulation: determine if the product is PNS-covered, the certification type required (PS Mark / ICC / SOC / exempt), the vendor&#x27;s certification posture, and the lead-time/cost impact on the new-product launch
Responsible (R): Product Compliance Manager / Merchandising
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per new SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3669_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3669_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3669_Task5" name="Product Compliance Manager gate assortment activation on certification…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Product Compliance Manager gate assortment activation on certification readiness: block SKU activation to sellable/PO-able until the PS License is verified (local) or the ICC plan is confirmed (import); manage exempt products with documented exemption basis
Responsible (R): Product Compliance Manager / MDM / Merchandising
Accountable (A): Product Compliance Manager
Duration: Per new SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3669_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3669_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3669_Task6" name="Product Compliance Manager/Import coordinate the certification path: trigger PS…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Product Compliance Manager/Import coordinate the certification path: trigger PS License application (vendor) or ICC/SOC import clearance (links to W3673), incorporate certification cost and lead-time into landed cost (links to VS-02.2/W144) and launch timing (links to VS-01.1), and confirm certification before first sale
Responsible (R): Product Compliance Manager / Import / Merchandising
Accountable (A): Product Compliance Manager
Duration: Per new SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3669_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3669_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3669_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3669_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-157 (ensure PS Mark / ICC certification coverage.) | - operational: early assessment and parallel certification; operational: MDM gating
Owner: Product Compliance Manager / Merchandising</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
